  "title": "Syabrubesi to Rasuwagadhi, five-day repeat (Pelican) — Post-event Imagery",
  "description": "Very-high-resolution Pelican coverage acquired 05:06 UTC on 1 September 2026, six days after the flood — a three-frame strip on essentially the same footprint as the 27 August Pelican collects, 98% of which it re-images. This is the only same-sensor, same-target sub-metre repeat in the catalog, five days apart, and the basis for change detection at roughly 0.56 m. Conditions are markedly better than the 27 August pass at the northern end: the frame over Rasuwagadhi reports 47% cloud and 31% clear, against 0% clear for all three 27 August frames. The two southern frames remain heavily obscured at 4% and 2% clear. The scoured river channel is traceable through the full height of the strip. 3 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened, udm2 assets.",
